{{ 'vishesh-sections.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{% comment %}
  Our Journey. An alternating spine timeline: a vertical line down the
  middle with milestone cards stepping left and right off it, each with
  its year, an era motif and its copy.

  This replaces a sticky one-at-a-time stage. That mechanic worked, but
  its shape was the problem rather than its implementation: a single
  short milestone card held inside a viewport-tall stuck stage always
  leaves a large empty band, and every attempt to close it only moved
  the emptiness around - centre it and you get two cream bands, stretch
  the card and you get one white one. It also had to fight Dawn's
  reveal-on-scroll header for the top of the viewport, which is what
  cropped the card on phones.

  Laying the nine milestones out in flow removes the whole class of
  problem: there is no stage to fill, nothing is position:sticky, no
  scroll is taken from the user, and the section is exactly as tall as
  its content. It also suits the content better - a fifty year family
  history reads as one continuous line rather than nine slides a reader
  has to scrub through to see.

  The spine is drawn: assets/vishesh-journey-path.js measures the nodes
  and builds an SVG path that threads through them, bowing to alternate
  sides between milestones, then traces it with stroke-dashoffset as the
  section scrolls. That is an enhancement on top of a finished section -
  the plain CSS track below stays as the fallback and the nodes ship
  fully coloured, so if the script never runs nothing is hidden.

  Items also ease in via the theme's existing data-animate="fade-up"
  hook. Both it and the path are gated on prefers-reduced-motion.
{% endcomment %}
<script src="{{ 'vishesh-journey-path.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<div class="vishesh-journey color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient" data-journey>
  <div class="page-width">
    <header class="vishesh-journey__head">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <span class="vishesh-journey__eyebrow" data-animate="fade-up">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="vishesh-journey__heading" data-animate="fade-up">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}
    </header>

    {% comment %}
      The path lives beside the list rather than inside it: an <svg> is
      not a permitted child of <ol>, and as a child it also shifted every
      milestone's :nth-child parity, which flipped the alternation.
    {% endcomment %}
    <div class="vishesh-journey__track" data-journey-list>
      {% comment %}
        Two copies of the same path: a faint track that is always there,
        and the brand-coloured line drawn over it on scroll. Sharing one
        `d` means they cannot drift out of alignment. Both are written by
        the script; empty until then, which is why the CSS spine sits
        underneath as the no-JS fallback.
      {% endcomment %}
      <svg class="vishesh-journey__path" data-journey-path aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path class="vishesh-journey__path-track" data-journey-track fill="none" />
        <path class="vishesh-journey__path-line" data-journey-line fill="none" />
        {%- comment -%}
          The head of the drawn line, moved along the path as it draws.
          The stroke alone advances too slowly to read as motion; a dot
          at the tip is what makes it obvious the line is being drawn.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <circle class="vishesh-journey__path-head-glow" data-journey-head-glow r="9" cx="0" cy="0" />
        <circle class="vishesh-journey__path-head" data-journey-head r="4.5" cx="0" cy="0" />
      </svg>

      <ol class="vishesh-journey__list" role="list">
        {%- assign last_era = '' -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {% comment %}
            Decade markers, derived from the years rather than authored,
            so they stay correct if the merchant edits or reorders
            milestones. They break fifty years into chapters instead of
            nine identical rows. Decorative - every year is already
            stated on its own milestone - so they are hidden from
            assistive tech rather than announced as list items.
          {% endcomment %}
          {%- assign era = block.settings.year | slice: 0, 3 | append: '0s' -%}
          {%- if era != last_era -%}
            <li class="vishesh-journey__era" aria-hidden="true" data-animate="fade-up">
              <span class="vishesh-journey__era-label">{{ era }}</span>
            </li>
            {%- assign last_era = era -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          <li class="vishesh-journey__item" data-animate="fade-up" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <div class="vishesh-journey__aside">
              <span class="vishesh-journey__motif" aria-hidden="true">
                {%- render 'vishesh-timeline-icon', icon: block.settings.icon -%}
              </span>
              <span class="vishesh-journey__year">{{ block.settings.year }}</span>
              <span class="vishesh-journey__index" aria-hidden="true">
                {{- forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }} / {{ forloop.length | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 -}}
              </span>
            </div>

            <span class="vishesh-journey__node" data-journey-node aria-hidden="true"></span>

            <div class="vishesh-journey__body">
              <p class="vishesh-journey__text">{{ block.settings.text }}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Vishesh Timeline",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "1970 to today"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Our Journey"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "scheme-2"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "milestone",
      "name": "Milestone",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "year", "label": "Year" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Text" },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "icon",
          "label": "Era motif",
          "default": "tin",
          "info": "Line drawing shown in this milestone's node on the line.",
          "options": [
            { "value": "tin", "label": "Masala tin" },
            { "value": "factory", "label": "Production unit" },
            { "value": "cart", "label": "Bullock cart" },
            { "value": "people", "label": "Next generation" },
            { "value": "certificate", "label": "Certification" },
            { "value": "pack", "label": "Consumer pack" },
            { "value": "network", "label": "Distribution" },
            { "value": "star", "label": "New brand" },
            { "value": "facility", "label": "Modern facility" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Vishesh Timeline",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "milestone",
          "settings": { "year": "1970", "text": "Humble start with a small rented production unit at Udhna, Surat." }
        },
        {
          "type": "milestone",
          "settings": { "year": "1971", "text": "Extended our production unit, manufacturing only Hing for five years." }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
